seal     : An add-on that bolted under the Genesis, the Sega CD added a CD-ROM drive, a second 68000, extra RAM, and a graphics ASIC for scaling and rotation. It opened the door to CD audio and full-motion-video games — and to the moral panic over titles like Night Trap.
